[E-PARTIAL] Error: a computation that might not finish can't run here
    ╭─[ reject/partial-row-total-body.sw:21:50 ]
    │
 15 │ def viaJob (f: () → {Fail | e} Nat): {e} Nat := runJob (MkJob f)
    │                                                               ┬  
    │                                                               ╰── `viaJob`'s body needs its row to be total here
    │ 
 21 │ def partialJob(): {Partial} Nat := viaJob (() => spin 0)
    │                                                  ───┬──  
    │                                                     ╰──── `spin` is `Partial`: it might not finish
    │ 
    │ Note 1: code whose type doesn't say `Partial` must finish, so it can't run anything that might not; if this is a function's body, add `Partial` to its type (`-> {Partial} …`); if it is a callback, the function taking it must allow a partial callback
    │ 
    │ Note 2: `viaJob` takes only total callbacks: its body puts a callback where only total code can go (a field of a data type, say), so its row variable stands for total rows only
────╯
